.TH "CSDLC-ISSUE" "1" "September 11, 2026" "C-SDLC v3" "ADL Operator Manual"
.SH NAME
csdlc\-issue \- retired preparation writer; use prepare intent
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\&csdlc prepare ISSUE \-\-plan PLAN.json
\&csdlc prepare \-\-intent\-request REQUEST.json
\&csdlc issue \-\-help
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
\&The direct issue \-\-request writer is retired and fails before request parsing or effects. Use prepare with an issue number and reviewed plan, or an exact generated \-\-intent\-request. The issue command remains discoverable through \-\-help and \-\-describe for migration.
.SH EFFECTS
\&Discovery is read\-only. Current preparation effects belong to the semantic prepare intent and its native transaction owner.
.SH OPTIONS
\&\-\-plan: Required semantic plan JSON for ordinary prepare.
.PP
\&\-\-intent\-request: Exact generated semantic request or wrapper.
.PP
\&\-\-request, \-\-registry, \-\-registrations, \-\-v3\-state\-root: Retired writer inputs documented only for migration discovery.
.PP
\&\-\-repo\-root: Select repository discovery for the semantic intent.
.PP
\&\-\-help: Show migration guidance; \-h is equivalent.
.SH REQUEST
\&Use csdlc.v3.intent_request.v1 for advanced execution. LocalPreparationRequest is a retired direct\-writer input and grants no CLI mutation authority.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
\&csdlc prepare 870 \-\-plan plan.json
.fi
.SH RECOVERY
\&Preserve index, values and transaction bytes. Reissue the exact interrupted mutating issue/bind/edit request through its native owner after checking the bound topology; do not use diagnostics as a repair command. If current recovery is denied, retain the finding and route a bounded tooling repair. Never hand\-edit transaction stages/backups or stale digest guards.
.SH SEE ALSO
\&csdlc(1), csdlc\-requests(1), csdlc\-workflow(1).
